 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "X0HJ5T58BAAJ",
   "from": "Tatum Mortimer",
   "author": "611f41cc873cf6fa",
   "date": "2016-09-08T19:39:50Z",
   "subject": "coloring internal branches using attached data",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><font color=\"#000000\">I&#39;d like to color my branches based on some data I have that can&#39;t be read in using one of ggtree&#39;s functions, so I&#39;m using %&lt;+% to attach the data. Unfortunately, the branches are only colored for the tips, but not the internal nodes. I got the internal node numbers following this example: <span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">ggtree</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">(</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">tree</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">)</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">+</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">geom_text2</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">(</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">aes</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">(</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">subset</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">=</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">!</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">isTip</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">, </span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">label</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">=</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">node</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">)</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">, </span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">hjust</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">=</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">-</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">.3</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">)</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">+</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">geom_tiplab</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">(</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;box-sizing:border-box;background-color:transparent\">).</span></font><div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">Here&#39;s an example of my code:</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">p &lt;- ggtree(tree, aes(color =log10(omega))) %&lt;+% results +</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">    geom_tiplab(size=3) + </font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">    geom_treescale() + </font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">    scale_color_viridis() + </font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">    theme(legend.position=&quot;right&quot;)</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">results is a data frame with the node labels (names for the tips, numbers for the internal nodes) in the first column and values I&#39;d like to color the branches by in the second column.</font></div></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><div>&gt; head(results)</div><div>                                     V1                           omega            p</div><div>1 Nocardia_brasiliensis_ATCC700358_esx1  0.000000     1.000000e+00</div><div>2 Nocardia_brasiliensis_ATCC700358_esxN  0.000000    1.922514e-01</div><div>3    Nocardia_cyriacigeorgica_GUH2_esxN    6.488117    2.580282e-06</div><div>4           Nocardia_farcinica_IFM_esxN         3.375098    7.255922e-06</div><div>5                                    77                        33.906093   8.611692e-09</div><div>6                                    76                        19.637654   0.000000e+00</div></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">I&#39;ve attached an image of the results currently. Is there any way to get the internal branches colored as well? </font></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "aKR4cvGRBAAJ",
   "from": "gc...@connect.hku.hk",
   "author": "f0dc0fdb872722c6",
   "date": "2016-09-09T02:17:26Z",
   "subject": "Re: coloring internal branches using attached data",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">by default, the data (results here) will be merged by label (tip &amp; node label) be default unless a column named &#39;node&#39; exists. In that case, it will merged by &#39;node&#39; number.<br><br>So, convert the 1st column to &#39;node&#39; number and stored in an additional column called &#39;node&#39; will solve this issue.<br><br>results$node &lt;- NA<br>tipnode &lt;- seq_along(tree$tip.label)<br>names(tipnode) &lt;- tree$tip.label<br>results$node &lt;- tipnode[results$V1] ## convert the tip label to tip node number<br>i &lt;- <a href=\"http://is.na\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://is.na&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482905540000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0eoQa1idvbLtC6DYeRpj2t\">is.na</a>(results$node)<br>results$node[i] = results$V1[i] ## fill in internal node number</div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br><div><font color=\"#000000\">p &lt;- ggtree(tree, aes(color =log10(omega))) %&lt;+% results +</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">    geom_tiplab(size=3) + </font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">    geom_treescale() + </font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">    scale_color_viridis() + </font></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><font color=\"#000000\">    theme(legend.position=&quot;right&quot;)<br><br><br></font>see also <a href=\"https://github.com/GuangchuangYu/ggtree/issues/47\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/GuangchuangYu/ggtree/issues/47&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482905540000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2YWmGQ7B9YYqgphVHC-c_D\">https://github.com/GuangchuangYu/ggtree/issues/47</a>, which provides another solution by using phylo4d.<br><br><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>On Friday, September 9, 2016 at 3:39:50 AM UTC+8, Tatum Mortimer wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><font color=\"#000000\">I&#39;d like to color my branches based on some data I have that can&#39;t be read in using one of ggtree&#39;s functions, so I&#39;m using %&lt;+% to attach the data. Unfortunately, the branches are only colored for the tips, but not the internal nodes. I got the internal node numbers following this example: <span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">ggtree</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">(</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">tree</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">)</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">+</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">geom_text2</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">(</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">aes</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">(</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">subset</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">=</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">!</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">isTip</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">, </span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">label</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">=</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">node</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">)</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">, </span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">hjust</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">=</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">-</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">.3</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">)</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">+</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\"> </span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">geom_tiplab</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">(</span><span style=\"font-size:inherit;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.42857;background-color:transparent\">).</span></font><div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">Here&#39;s an example of my code:</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">p &lt;- ggtree(tree, aes(color =log10(omega))) %&lt;+% results +</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">    geom_tiplab(size=3) + </font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">    geom_treescale() + </font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">    scale_color_viridis() + </font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">    theme(legend.position=&quot;right&quot;)</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">results is a data frame with the node labels (names for the tips, numbers for the internal nodes) in the first column and values I&#39;d like to color the branches by in the second column.</font></div></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><div>&gt; head(results)</div><div>                                     V1                           omega            p</div><div>1 Nocardia_brasiliensis_ATCC700358_esx1  0.000000     1.000000e+00</div><div>2 Nocardia_brasiliensis_ATCC700358_esxN  0.000000    1.922514e-01</div><div>3    Nocardia_cyriacigeorgica_GUH2_esxN    6.488117    2.580282e-06</div><div>4           Nocardia_farcinica_IFM_esxN         3.375098    7.255922e-06</div><div>5                                    77                        33.906093   8.611692e-09</div><div>6                                    76                        19.637654   0.000000e+00</div></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\">I&#39;ve attached an image of the results currently. Is there any way to get the internal branches colored as well? </font></div><div><br></div><